    task: "Clarion Freight wants one shared recursion guard for all handlers.\nWrite class `RecursionGuard` with:\n- `public static Set<Id> filterNew(String key, Set<Id> recordIds)`: returns the Ids NOT yet processed under that key, and marks them as processed\n- Keys are independent, e.g. 'Account.afterUpdate' vs 'Contact.afterInsert'\n- Store state in a static Map<String, Set<Id>>\n- Null or empty input returns an empty set\n- A `@TestVisible` static `reset()` that clears everything",
    starter: "public with sharing class RecursionGuard {\n    public static Set<Id> filterNew(String key, Set<Id> recordIds) {\n        // TODO\n        return null;\n    }\n}\n",
    solution: "public with sharing class RecursionGuard {\n    private static final Map<String, Set<Id>> PROCESSED = new Map<String, Set<Id>>();\n\n    public static Set<Id> filterNew(String key, Set<Id> recordIds) {\n        Set<Id> fresh = new Set<Id>();\n        if (recordIds == null || recordIds.isEmpty()) {\n            return fresh;\n        }\n        if (!PROCESSED.containsKey(key)) {\n            PROCESSED.put(key, new Set<Id>());\n        }\n        Set<Id> seen = PROCESSED.get(key);\n        for (Id recordId : recordIds) {\n            if (!seen.contains(recordId)) {\n                fresh.add(recordId);\n            }\n        }\n        seen.addAll(fresh);\n        return fresh;\n    }\n\n    @TestVisible\n    private static void reset() {\n        PROCESSED.clear();\n    }\n}\n",
