    task: "Elstree Care Homes wants handler logic testable without DML.\nWrite `CaseTriggerHandler` with constructor `(List<Case> newList, Map<Id, Case> oldMap, System.TriggerOperation operation)` and `run()` that switches on the operation:\n- BEFORE_INSERT: blank Origin → 'Web'\n- BEFORE_UPDATE: when Status changes to 'Closed' and Resolution__c is blank, field error on Resolution__c\nTrigger `CaseTrigger` (before insert, before update): `new CaseTriggerHandler(Trigger.new, Trigger.oldMap, Trigger.operationType).run();`\nAdd test class `CaseTriggerHandlerTest` that calls the handler directly (no DML) for both events, using the Assert class and hasErrors(). No hard-coded Ids.",
    starter: "public with sharing class CaseTriggerHandler {\n    public CaseTriggerHandler(List<Case> newList, Map<Id, Case> oldMap, System.TriggerOperation operation) {\n        // TODO\n    }\n\n    public void run() {\n        // TODO\n    }\n}\n\ntrigger CaseTrigger on Case (before insert, before update) {\n    // TODO\n}\n\n@IsTest\nprivate class CaseTriggerHandlerTest {\n    // TODO\n}\n",
    solution: "public with sharing class CaseTriggerHandler {\n    private final List<Case> newList;\n    private final Map<Id, Case> oldMap;\n    private final System.TriggerOperation operation;\n\n    public CaseTriggerHandler(List<Case> newList, Map<Id, Case> oldMap, System.TriggerOperation operation) {\n        this.newList = newList;\n        this.oldMap = oldMap;\n        this.operation = operation;\n    }\n\n    public void run() {\n        switch on operation {\n            when BEFORE_INSERT {\n                beforeInsert();\n            }\n            when BEFORE_UPDATE {\n                beforeUpdate();\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    private void beforeInsert() {\n        for (Case c : newList) {\n            if (String.isBlank(c.Origin)) {\n                c.Origin = 'Web';\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    private void beforeUpdate() {\n        for (Case c : newList) {\n            Case oldCase = oldMap.get(c.Id);\n            if (c.Status == 'Closed' && oldCase.Status != 'Closed' && String.isBlank(c.Resolution__c)) {\n                c.Resolution__c.addError('Add a resolution before closing the case.');\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\ntrigger CaseTrigger on Case (before insert, before update) {\n    new CaseTriggerHandler(Trigger.new, Trigger.oldMap, Trigger.operationType).run();\n}\n\n@IsTest\nprivate class CaseTriggerHandlerTest {\n    private static Id fakeCaseId() {\n        return Id.valueOf(Case.SObjectType.getDescribe().getKeyPrefix() + '000000000001');\n    }\n\n    @IsTest\n    static void beforeInsertDefaultsOrigin() {\n        Case c = new Case(Subject = 'Boiler fault');\n        new CaseTriggerHandler(new List<Case>{ c }, null, System.TriggerOperation.BEFORE_INSERT).run();\n        Assert.areEqual('Web', c.Origin, 'Origin should default to Web');\n    }\n\n    @IsTest\n    static void closingWithoutResolutionIsBlocked() {\n        Id caseId = fakeCaseId();\n        Case oldCase = new Case(Id = caseId, Status = 'New');\n        Case newCase = new Case(Id = caseId, Status = 'Closed');\n        new CaseTriggerHandler(\n            new List<Case>{ newCase },\n            new Map<Id, Case>{ caseId => oldCase },\n            System.TriggerOperation.BEFORE_UPDATE\n        ).run();\n        Assert.isTrue(newCase.hasErrors(), 'Closing without a resolution should add an error');\n    }\n}\n",
    checks: [{ re: /switch\s+on\s+\w+/i, msg: "run() switches on the injected operation" }, { re: /Trigger\.operationType/i, msg: "Trigger passes Trigger.operationType" }, { re: /TriggerOperation\.BEFORE_INSERT/i, msg: "Test calls the handler with BEFORE_INSERT" }, { re: /Assert\.\w+\s*\(/i, msg: "Uses the Assert class" }, { re: /hasErrors\s*\(\s*\)/i, msg: "Checks the error with hasErrors()" }],
    forbid: [{ re: /System\.assert(Equals|NotEquals)?\s*\(/i, msg: "Use the Assert class instead of System.assert" }, { re: /'(001|003|006|00Q|500)[A-Za-z0-9]{12,15}'/, msg: "No hard-coded record Ids" }, { re: /\b(insert|update|delete|upsert)\s+\w+\s*;/i, msg: "No DML needed — change Trigger.new directly in a before trigger" }],
    hints: ["Store the three constructor arguments in final fields and switch on the operation in run().", "Build a fake Id from Case.SObjectType.getDescribe().getKeyPrefix() + 12 zeros/digits.", "SObject.hasErrors() is true after addError, even outside a real trigger."],
    ai: "Verify the handler has no direct dependency on Trigger.* (only the trigger passes context), both events are tested without DML, Assert is used, and no Ids are hard-coded."
