    task: "Calder Shipping Group lets admins plug handlers in without code changes.\n- Interface `ITriggerHandler` with `void handle(System.TriggerOperation operation, List<SObject> newList, Map<Id, SObject> oldMap)`\n- `TriggerDispatcher.run(Schema.SObjectType objectType)`: load active `Trigger_Handler__mdt` records (Object__c = object API name, Handler_Class__c, Order__c, Active__c) in Order__c order; instantiate each with Type.forName and call handle() with the trigger context\n- Unknown class name → throw a custom TriggerDispatcherException naming the class\n- `AccountTrigger` on all 7 events calls `TriggerDispatcher.run(Account.SObjectType)`",
    starter: "public interface ITriggerHandler {\n    // TODO\n}\n\npublic with sharing class TriggerDispatcher {\n    public static void run(Schema.SObjectType objectType) {\n        // TODO\n    }\n}\n\ntrigger AccountTrigger on Account (before insert, before update, before delete, after insert, after update, after delete, after undelete) {\n    // TODO\n}\n",
    solution: "public interface ITriggerHandler {\n    void handle(System.TriggerOperation operation, List<SObject> newList, Map<Id, SObject> oldMap);\n}\n\npublic with sharing class TriggerDispatcher {\n    public class TriggerDispatcherException extends Exception {}\n\n    public static void run(Schema.SObjectType objectType) {\n        String objectName = objectType.getDescribe().getName();\n        List<Trigger_Handler__mdt> configs = [\n            SELECT Handler_Class__c FROM Trigger_Handler__mdt\n            WHERE Object__c = :objectName AND Active__c = true\n            ORDER BY Order__c ASC\n        ];\n        for (Trigger_Handler__mdt config : configs) {\n            Type handlerType = Type.forName(config.Handler_Class__c);\n            if (handlerType == null) {\n                throw new TriggerDispatcherException('Handler class not found: ' + config.Handler_Class__c);\n            }\n            ITriggerHandler handler = (ITriggerHandler) handlerType.newInstance();\n            handler.handle(Trigger.operationType, Trigger.new, Trigger.oldMap);\n        }\n    }\n}\n\ntrigger AccountTrigger on Account (before insert, before update, before delete, after insert, after update, after delete, after undelete) {\n    TriggerDispatcher.run(Account.SObjectType);\n}\n",
    checks: [{ re: /void\s+handle\s*\(\s*(System\.)?TriggerOperation\s+\w+\s*,\s*List<\s*SObject\s*>\s+\w+\s*,\s*Map<\s*Id\s*,\s*SObject\s*>\s+\w+\s*\)/i, msg: "ITriggerHandler declares handle(TriggerOperation, List<SObject>, Map<Id, SObject>)" }, { re: /Trigger_Handler__mdt/i, msg: "Reads Trigger_Handler__mdt" }, { re: /Order__c/i, msg: "Runs handlers in Order__c order" }, { re: /Type\.forName\s*\(/i, msg: "Resolves the class with Type.forName" }, { re: /newInstance\s*\(\s*\)/i, msg: "Instantiates the handler with newInstance()" }, { re: /extends\s+Exception/i, msg: "Defines a custom exception for unknown classes" }],
